2.
Definitions. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,
(a)
Force means the Railway Protection Force constituted under section 3 of the Railway Protection Force Act, 1957 (
23 of 1957
);
(b)
member of the Force means a person appointed to the Force, other than a superior officer;
(c)
officer of the Force means an officer of and above the rank of Assistant Sub-Inspector appointed to the Force and
includes a superior officer;
(d)
railway property includes any goods, money or valuable security or animal, belonging to, or in the charge or possession
of, a railway administration;
(e)
superior officer means any of the officers appointed under section 4 of the Railway Protection Force Act, 1957 (
23 of 1957
), and includes any other officer appointed by the Central Government as a superior officer of the Force;
(f)
